From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: rtnetlink: export rtmsg_ifinfo for the ASK PPP hooks

The ASK PPP fast-path hook (patch 070) calls rtmsg_ifinfo() from
ppp_generic to announce the offloaded PPPoE link. OpenWrt builds
ppp_generic as a module (kmod-ppp), and mainline does not export
rtmsg_ifinfo, so modpost fails:

  ERROR: modpost: "rtmsg_ifinfo" [drivers/net/ppp/ppp_generic.ko] undefined!

The NXP LSDK kernel exports the symbol; restore that export (mainline
carried it too until the last in-tree caller went away). CPE_FAST_PATH=n
builds compile the hook out, so this only matters for the ASK image.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
--- a/net/core/rtnetlink.c
+++ b/net/core/rtnetlink.c
@@ -4265,6 +4265,7 @@
 	rtmsg_ifinfo_event(type, dev, change, rtnl_get_event(0), flags,
 			   NULL, 0, portid, nlh);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(rtmsg_ifinfo);
 
 void rtmsg_ifinfo_newnet(int type, struct net_device *dev, unsigned int change,
 			 gfp_t flags, int *new_nsid, int new_ifindex)
